**StoryRef:** AMSD-1820

When fixing code via WriteFile replacement of an existing file, always diff the new content against the original to ensure no assignment LHS is dropped. A dangling ternary like `? 'a' : 'b';` (without the `x =` prefix) compiles to TS1128 "Declaration or statement expected". When a previous attempt left a fragmentary expression in place, reconstruct the full statement rather than just deleting the dangling lines — the lines were almost certainly the RHS of a missing assignment.
